From b4fcd85ea20bfb6886df02dd14e5e36cd10863eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikita Konton <kontonkara@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 02:09:54 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add per-output scaling-mode config and IPC action

Expose the "scaling mode" DRM connector property, which controls how the
display engine scales a mode that doesn't match the native resolution of
the panel: "full" (stretch), "full-aspect", "center" or "none".

It is set together with the other connector properties (max bpc, HDR
reset) on connect, on session resume and on every output config change,
so it persists across mode changes and hotplug and is committed before
the new mode is applied. When unset, niri doesn't touch the property.

Also add `niri msg output <name> scaling-mode <mode>` and report the
current scaling mode in `niri msg outputs`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
